<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105548" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροφ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who brings up, foster-father,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				344
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theophil.
				1
			</span></i>; <i>tutor,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					148.2
				</span></i>
			 (Cyprus, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				256.1
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				1568.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.664
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				5.31
			</span></i>; of a woman, <i>nurse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				760
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφεύς</span> codd.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				863
			</span></i>, Ajax addresses the plains and fountains of Troy, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίρετ᾽ ὦ τροφῆς ἐμοί</span>
			<i>ye who have fed</i> me, or <i>with whom</i> I <i>have
			lived</i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροφέας παρέδωκε τὴν γῆν καὶ τὴν
					θάλασσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					4.1.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>rearer, breeder,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					735b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅρματος τ.</span>
			<i>one who keeps</i> a chariot, ib.<i><span class="en">
				834b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσης κακίας</span>
			<i>one who fosters</i> all wickedness, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				580a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>one who gives free meals to the people,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IGRom.
				3.89
			</span></i> (Amastris, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				4.1680
			</span></i> (Pergam.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>personal attendant, slave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				49(25).3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				50(26).103
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
